$COMMENT  ***********************************************************************  *     This file is a so-called "Info" file describing a piece of      *  *   software in a standarized way using EFFO's "Info" file format.    *  *     The format provides all basic information about a program       *  *   in a well structured manner allowing automatic extraction         *  *   of important short-form data for databases and software lists     *  *   but including more detailed descriptions as well.                 *  *     The structure is formed by a set of keywords dividing the       *  *   information into different paragraphs (see syntax description     *  *   below).                                                           *  *                                                                     *  *     All programs distributed by EFFO will include such a file.      *  *   It will be called Info_xxxx, where xxxx is the program's name.    *  *   EFFO encourages all its members and all forum participants as     *  *   well as commercial suppliers of OS-9 and OS-9000 software to      *  *   use this format to describe their software.                       *  *     An empty "form" for Info files called "Info_empty_form" will    *  *   be distributed with all EFFO disk and through the OS9-BBS.        *  *                                                                     *  *     The syntax is quite simple: Each paragraph begins with a        *  *   "keyword line" which is a line with a $-Sign in the very first    *  *   column immediately followed by the keyword itself. The rest of    *  *   the line is reserved for short comments about the paragraph's     *  *   purpose. Some paragaphs are mandatory, and some are restricted    *  *   in size to ensure that reliable database entries can be           *  *   extracted from the file.                                          *  *     All subseqent lines up to the next keyword line (or the         *  *   end-of-file) are forming the paragraph body, i.e the information  *  *   that belongs to the keyword.                                      *  *     The order in which the keywords appear in the text (if they     *  *   appear at all for optional paragraphs) is free with one           *  *   important exception: "$PROGRAM-NAME" must always be the first     *  *   keyword in the program description. This rule allows multiple     *  *   descriptions to be merged into a single text file without using   *  *   special delimiters in between.                                    *  *     Finally, "$COMMENT" paragraphs are provided to include          *  *   any information not related to a program description, like        *  *   this text. They can appear anywhere in the file, even before      *  *   the first "$PROGRAM-NAME".                                        *  ***********************************************************************$PROGRAM-NAME  Name of the program (FIRST KEYWORD, <=20 chars, mandatory)  help$VERSION  Current version/revision/edition information (<=20 chars, optional)  1.0 Ed#3$PURPOSE  What is the program/package for ? (<=50 chars, mandatory)  Extended on-line help for OS-9/68k$SUMMARY  Short summary. (<=3 lines of <=80 chars each, mandatory)  The advanced HELP utility offers structured access to all type of help  texts in OS-9/68k systems. The program replaces the standard utility  called "help".$KEYWORDS  Keywords for database, comma separated (<20 chars each, recommended)  help, online, information$PROJECT  Info, if the program is part of a bigger project (no limit, optional)$STATUS  Program status (final, beta, experimental etc) (no limit, optional)  first released version, final$REFERENCES  Other programs/infos related to this program (no limit, optional)  helpindex$HARDWARE  System hardware dependencies (no limit, mandatory if any)$SCREEN-INTERFACE  Termcap, Zterm, etc. (<40 chars, mandatory if not raw-I/O)$PREREQUISITES  Non-system specific Hardware/Software required (no limit, opt.)$OS-VERSION  Required/Supported OS (Type, Version, Revision) (<80 chars, opt.)  OS-9/68k V1.2 or higher, OS-9000 planned$DOCUMENTATION  Type and language of documentation (<80 chars, mandatory)  Help file and Read_Me in english.$RUNTIME-FILES  Paths of the files required at run-time (no limit, optional)  CMDS/help         The help utility  CMDS/helpindex    Index file creator utility  SYS/HELP/help.hlp The help file for help itself (=documentation)  SYS/HELP/*.hlp    Additional help files  SYS/HELP/*.hlib   Additional help libraries$DOCUMENTATION-FILES  Paths of documentation files (no limit, optional)  Read_Me           general information  Info              This File  SYS/HELP/help.hlp A help file describing help itself$SOURCE-LANGUAGE  Programming Language(s) used (<30 chars, mandatory)  C$SOURCE-AVAILABILITY  Avaliability of source code (<30 chars, mandatory)  Full source$SOURCE-FILES  Paths of the source files (no limit, optional)  help.c            Source for the help utility  helpindex.c       Source for the helpindex utility$SOURCE-PREREQUISITES  Libraries, files, compilers required (no limit, opt.)  Microware C V3.0$COMPILATION        How to compile the program (no limit, optional)  cc help.c   or  cc helpindex.c , resp.$AUTHOR-NAME  Name(s) ONLY of the author(s). (<=80 chars, mandatory)  Lukas Zeller$AUTHOR-INFO  Additional information about the author(s) (no limit, optional)  Hofenstrasse 12  CH-8708 Maennedorf  eMail:  zeller@ethz.uucp          zeller@strati.ethz.ch          ...cernvax!ethz!zeller  DECNet: 57390::ZELLER (PSI%4991108411::STRATI::ZELLER)$AVAILABILITY  Public, Shareware, Commercial ? (<=30 chars, mandatory)  Public domain$CONDITIONS  Conditions, e.g. Shareware fee (no limit, optional)  1. This Program may only be used for peaceful applications. I do NOT     ALLOW using this program for anything that has to do with dev